==============================================================================
2b. FINDINGS - what it is, how serious, and what kind of problem
==============================================================================

F1  SENS-07 soil_temp_c is Fahrenheit, not Celsius   [SENS-07]
    detected : jitter ratio 1.82 vs fleet; /1.8 gives 0.400 exactly; mean and sd also match after conversion
    severity : high    class: data problem - unit error
    next     : convert to Celsius; ask firmware whether the payload or the conversion is wrong

F2  SENS-07 on a +2h clock, and DD/MM while the fleet is ISO   [SENS-07]
    detected : light cross-correlation 0.802 -> 0.9997 when shifted 2h
    severity : high    class: data problem - clock/timezone
    next     : ask firmware; testable - a timezone offset becomes +1h in winter

F3  SENS-06 moisture frozen at exactly 25.01 for 14 days   [SENS-06]
    detected : longest constant run 1344 samples; its other four channels all keep moving
    severity : high    class: sensor fault - dead channel
    next     : null the frozen window; do not treat 25.01 as a reading

F4  SENS-03 EC climbs monotonically, no logged cause   [SENS-03]
    detected : a straight climb from 06-11 -- see the drift fit in the evidence above for the onset, rate and R2; 354 out-of-range readings in 17 runs, 346 of them inside a run (longest 307), only 8 isolated; no fertilising log near onset; the four devices that WERE fertilised show no EC response (section 6a)
    severity : high    class: sensor fault - drift
    next     : exclude EC for this device, or recalibrate; ask calibration whether a straight-line climb is possible

F5  SENS-04 moisture exceeds the instrument's specified 65% ceiling   [SENS-04]
    detected : 431 readings (21.4%) above 65%, peaking 107.12. Every one sits in a run of two or more -- 11 runs, longest 44, ZERO isolated -- so this is a sustained excursion, not glitches; jitter 0.47 vs 0.14 fleet; dry-down 38.4 %VWC/day vs 3-6 fleet (the Task 8 signal)
    severity : high    class: unknown - fault or different physical setup
    next     : measure pot size and probe seating, or gravimetric reference; ask horticulture

F6  SENS-08 emits single-sample values that cannot be explained   [SENS-08]
    detected : 22 are physically impossible -- 12 moisture below 0, 10 humidity above 100 -- and are emptied. 8 more are possible but implausible: a light reading at night, bracketed by zeros. The other seven devices read exactly 0 at all 8 moments, so it was not a shared light -- but a lamp near one pot would do it
    severity : low     class: 22 sensor artefacts; 8 unresolved
    next     : empty the impossible 22; keep and flag the 8 -- a real light would be deleted by emptying. Ask firmware at D13

F7  SENS-05 missing 193 slots (48.5h)   [SENS-05]
    detected : coverage ledger against the expected 15-min grid
    severity : medium  class: data problem - availability
    next     : leave the gap. The ~320-reading buffer makes 193 slots stay WITHIN capacity, so recovery was possible -- an upper bound, not evidence the readings survived. Whether they did needs transport telemetry, not arithmetic. Reported as absence; cause unresolved

F8  SENS-08 has 15 superfluous duplicate rows   [SENS-08]
    detected : identical payloads, 0 conflicting
    severity : low     class: data problem - at-least-once redelivery
    next     : deduplicate; lossless because nothing disagrees

F9  user_plant_id is not unique, so log/image joins multiply rows   [all]
    detected : contextual 49->67, images 28->35; the sensor join is clean, which is the trap
    severity : medium  class: schema problem
    next     : dedupe the mapping to one row per plant before joining

F10  Two plants have two sensors, and the pairs do not correlate   [UP-1001, UP-1003]
    detected : r = -0.076 and +0.103 over the full overlap; excluding SENS-06's 1,344 frozen samples the second is +0.140. Both are near zero, so the probes do not move together either way -- the frozen stretch pulls the figure toward zero rather than hiding a stronger relationship. Same-pot probes share a reservoir and must move together
    severity : high    class: unknown - real config or mapping bug
    next     : ask product whether the app allows two sensors per plant; do not average

F11  Watering logs and sensor events are unrelated   [all plants]
    detected : 31 of 34 watering logs have no moisture rise within 6h -- and 3 hits is below the ~3.5 expected by chance, so the matches carry no information. All four log types were tested against the channel their own event should move, and none lines up. LIGHT CONTRADICTS: 'Moved closer to window' moves the daily light peak DOWN by 4.4 on average, the opposite of what it claims (n=3, within the daily sd of 5.3 -- suggestive, not proof). The sensor's own rises land exactly on the hour -- 35 of 37 excluding SENS-08 -- while the logs are all at human times, so the two look independently generated
    severity : high    class: label problem
    next     : do not use logs as event ground truth; ask firmware whether the device does anything at 00:00

F12  Environment is near-identical across all eight devices   [all]
    detected : mean pairwise r on aligned time: light 0.991, temp 0.974, humidity 0.937 -- against moisture 0.201 and EC -0.005. Moisture is an order of magnitude lower because each pot is its own reservoir
    severity : medium  class: artefact - shared or generated ambient series
    next     : do not use 'differs from the fleet' as an anomaly test for temp/light/humidity

F13  substrate_label is a snapshot with no effective dating   [UP-1006]
    detected : one label per device for the whole window, yet UP-1006 logged 'Fresh substrate + repot' on 06-13 and the label never moves
    severity : medium  class: semantic problem - calibration parameter without history
    next     : ask whether that pot's substrate actually changed; if it did, pre-06-13 VWC was produced by a different conversion curve than this label implies

